tasks.instructions:
Read the candidate brief named as rank 1 in the charter. Decide which distinct approaches are worth building — usually two to four; the per-request ceiling is five. Two approaches that differ only in naming are one approach.

Then create one execution context per approach in a SINGLE expansion. Write the payload to `.cc/temp/expand.json`:

```json
{
  "requestId": "expand-candidates-1",
  "rationale": "<why this fan-out, in one sentence>",
  "contexts": [
    {
      "handle": "candidate-<short-approach-name>",
      "title": "Candidate: <approach>",
      "acceptanceCriteria": "<what has to be true for this candidate to count as built>",
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "approach": { "type": "string" },
          "score": { "type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 10 }
        },
        "required": ["approach", "score"],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "contextHandle": "candidate-<short-approach-name>",
      "title": "Build the <approach> candidate",
      "instructions": "<self-contained instructions: what to build, and to score it out of 10 against the brief's axes>"
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    { "from": "context-generate", "to": "candidate-<short-approach-name>" },
    { "from": "candidate-<short-approach-name>", "to": "context-filter" }
  ]
}
```

Every candidate needs BOTH edges: one from `context-generate` so it becomes eligible when you finish, and one into `context-filter` so the fan-out converges. A candidate with no edge into the filter is refused as unreachable work.

Submit it with `cctl workflow graph expand --file .cc/temp/expand.json`. The request id is single-use: if the command fails with a conflict, re-run it VERBATIM — an accepted expansion replays from its receipt and never fans out twice. If it is refused, fix what the refusal names and submit under a NEW request id.

The candidates inherit this context's gates but not its expansion authority, so the fan-out is one level deep. Do not add candidates in a second batch: one expansion is one proposition about the shape of the graph.

Finally, complete this task with a summary naming the approaches you chose and the request id you used.
